You have a few options:

1. **`@WithMockUser` (Recommended - Simplest)**
   ```java
   @Test
   @WithMockUser
   public void testAddLiftingExercise() throws Exception {
       // Your test code here
   }
   ```
   This automatically provides a mock authenticated user for that test, bypassing the 403 without needing bearer tokens.

2. **Class-level `@WithMockUser`** (Apply to all tests)
   ```java
   @SpringBootTest
   @AutoConfigureMockMvc
   @Transactional
   @WithMockUser
   public class LiftingExerciseControllerTest {
       // All tests will run as authenticated user
   }
   ```

3. **Disable security for specific tests** (Less common, but possible)
   ```java
   @Test
   public void testAddLiftingExercise() throws Exception {
       mvc.perform(post("/api/lifting")...)
           .with(SecurityMockMvcRequestPostProcessors.anonymous())
           // Only if your endpoint is truly public
